# The failover sweep's ratchet (ADR-0055 §11): every cell of the base
# catalogue that fails today, with the decision section that owns its
# correction. A change that makes a cell pass removes its line; a new failure
# is never added without its owner. The list only shrinks.
#
# The owner is read from the finding: a missing or extra CDR §5; a final
# under another tag than a provisional that left inside the replication
# window, a request a copy sends without the record of what the dead owner
# sent, and a request into a dialog the other copy ended §4; the non-2xx final
# of a dialled INVITE nobody ACKs §12; a PRACK, an owed ACK or an in-dialog
# request left unanswered §2; a 2xx repeat routed through the other owner §8;
# and any other finding of a split cell §7.

